Healing Progression
Healing remains a bottom-up process. Your body must fully clear the "noise" of minor injuries before it can mend deep trauma.
Clearing Scrapped: You heal 1 point every 15 minutes. Once the Scrapped pool is full, you are no longer "Scrapped" and can begin the long-term healing of Bruises.
Mending Bruised: Once Scrapped is full, you heal 1 point per day. Once the Bruised pool is full, the -1 dice penalty is removed, and you can begin the slow process of healing Wounds.
Recovering Wounded: Once Bruised is full, you heal 1 point every 7 days. Once the Wounded pool is full, the -2 dice penalty is removed.
________________________________________
Combat Example: Durability 10 (40 HP)
40 HP: Perfect health.
30 HP (Scrapped): No penalties. If you rest for 2.5 hours, you're back to 40.
20 HP (Bruised): You take a -1 dice penalty to everything. You must heal those 10 Scrapped points first (2.5 hours), then wait 1 day to reach 21 HP and remove the penalty.
10 HP (Wounded): You take a -2 dice penalty. You must heal 20 Scrapped points (5 hours) and 10 Bruised points (10 days) before you can even begin healing these wounds at a rate of one point per week.

Neither Storms: Updated Mitigation
Neither Storms are atmospheric surges that lose intensity as they penetrate deeper into the earth or are blocked by the Spire's massive structure.
Mitigation (Intensity Reduction)
The environmental intensity is lowered by the following cumulative factors:
•	Depth (Mines): -1 Intensity for every 100 feet below the surface. (At 300+ feet, storms have no effect).
•	Racial (Orc): -1 Intensity.
•	Layer: -1 Intensity if the storm occurs in the Neither (vs. the Dark Neither).
•	Structural: -1 Intensity if inside a reinforced structure (Spires, Hamlets).
•	Deep Spire Seal: -2 Intensity if in the lower levels of a Spire with all entrances hermetically sealed.
