Mining Safety Example
•	The Surface Mine (50 ft deep): No depth mitigation. In a Level 2 storm, workers without a sealed structure take 5 Stress and 1 Damage every hour.
•	The Shallow Shaft (100 ft deep): -1 Intensity from Depth. A Level 2 storm is re-duced to Level 1. Stress and damage only occur once per day.
•	The Deep Mine (300+ ft deep): -3 Intensity from Depth. Even a Level 3 storm is reduced to Level 0. The miners are completely safe from the storm's mechanical effects, though they may hear the "howl" of the Neither through the ventilation shafts.
