At the beginning of a new Story Arc, all players automatically receive 2 points of Perseverance.
Characters with the Determination (Will-based) skill can push themselves further:
•	The Determination Roll: At the start of the arc, roll a Determination Skill Test.
•	Bonus Points: For every Success generated on this roll, the character gains +1 additional point of Perseverance.
•	Note: Perseverance does not carry over between arcs. Use it or lose it.
________________________________________
II. Spending Perseverance
Perseverance can be "burnt" to achieve one of two specific mechanical advantages. You may spend multiple points on a single action if necessary.
1. The Second Chance (1 Point)
•	Effect: Reroll any Skill Test.
•	Context: You may use this after seeing the initial result of a roll. You must accept the re-sults of the second roll.
2. Defy the Odds (1 Point)
•	Effect: Treat a roll that has Disadvantage as a Normal 1-Die Roll instead.
•	Context: This is essential for characters who are Bruised (-1 Die) or Wounded (-2 Dice).
o	If you are Bruised (normally rolling 0 dice/disadvantage), spending 1 point allows you to roll 1 Die normally.
o	If you are Wounded (normally rolling 0 dice with even steeper disadvantage), spending 1 point brings you back to a standard 1-Die roll.
________________________________________
III. Strategic Utility
Perseverance creates a vital "emergency button" for the health system we’ve built:
•	Pushing Through Trauma: Since Wounded characters suffer a -2 dice penalty (often re-ducing them to rolling 0 dice), Perseverance is the only way to ensure a chance of success during a desperate escape or a final stand.
•	Consistency: For the Professional or Noble classes, burning a point to reroll a critical Ne-gotiation or Logic test can prevent a catastrophic drop in Status.
